Figure 2 shows an example of the visualization of the localization result used for navigation guidance. The scenario is that the mobile computer user is working in a large industrial building and the user is surrounded by huge containers, pipes, and other equipments. A ﬂoor-map of the working site is displayed in the main window of the application. There is a red dot showing the position of the user. A green line is shown on the ﬂoor-map as a navigation guidance.
We augment the real-time video with text and virtual objects to provide the mobile computer user with more information. For example, we can carpet the ﬂoor in the image with the ﬂoor map and put arrows on the ﬂoor as a navigation guidance, as shown in Figure 2.

